comments.body:
> [#18088 (comment)](https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/issues/18088#issuecomment-2277968519)

Ok, now I understand why you added explicit muzzy_decay_ms:-1

I've run the numpy vs polars comparison Wes [mentioned](https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/issues/18088), indeed polars is only on par with numpy when muzzy_decay_ms or dirty_decay_ms  are set to -1, otherwise it's x4.5 difference.

I've also run a search for good combinations of jemalloc params that can imitate timings of muzzy_decay_ms:-1 - without success.

But I can confirm that in my production workload OOMs stopped after I set muzzy_decay_ms:500.
Running time seems about the same though.

I think _RJEM_MALLOC_CONF and speed vs ram footprint tradeoff achieved via muzzy_decay_ms:-1 need to be documented, so that people don't create similar issues and just go straight to the solution, if their workloads are OOMing.

As for the real solution, I only see 3 options:

1) **FIXING JEMALLOC**

Looking at https://github.com/jemalloc/jemalloc/blob/dev/src/arena.c, muzzy decay is strictly coupled with dirty decay
```c

void arena_decay_dirty(...) {
    if (arena_decay_impl(...)) {  // Only if dirty decay did work
        arena_maybe_decay_muzzy(...);
    }
}
```

Looks like in sub_one-like scenarios muzzy decay never runs. It only runs when: Dirty decay completes fully (purges all dirty pages) AND there's still time remaining in the decay interval.

**AI suggests these steps:**

To achieve your goal of ensuring muzzy_decay_ms settings work independently (without being coupled to dirty page decay), here's how to modify jemalloc's source code:

1. Modify arena_decay_dirty() in src/arena.c
Original Code:

```c
void arena_decay_dirty(tsdn_t *tsdn, arena_t *arena, bool is_background_thread) {
    if (arena_decay_impl(tsdn, arena, &arena->decay_dirty, &arena->extents_dirty,
        is_background_thread)) {
        arena_maybe_decay_muzzy(tsdn, arena, is_background_thread);
    }
}
```
Modified Code:


```c
void arena_decay_dirty(tsdn_t *tsdn, arena_t *arena, bool is_background_thread) {
    // Always process dirty decay
    arena_decay_impl(tsdn, arena, &arena->decay_dirty, &arena->extents_dirty,
        is_background_thread);

    // Always attempt muzzy decay regardless of dirty decay outcome
    arena_maybe_decay_muzzy(tsdn, arena, is_background_thread);
}
```

2. Create a New Background Thread Function (Optional but Recommended)
Add to src/background_thread.c:

```c
static void
background_thread_muzzy_work(tsd_t *tsd) {
    arena_t *arena;
    unsigned narenas = narenas_total_get();

    for (unsigned i = 0; i < narenas; i++) {
        arena = arena_get(tsd_tsdn(tsd), i, false);
        if (arena) {
            arena_maybe_decay_muzzy(tsd_tsdn(tsd), arena, true);
        }
    }
}
```
3. Hook into Background Thread Processing
Modify background_thread0_work() in src/background_thread.c:


```c
static void
background_thread0_work(tsd_t *tsd) {
    // Existing dirty decay work
    background_thread_dirty_work(tsd);

    // NEW: Add muzzy-specific processing
    background_thread_muzzy_work(tsd);
}
```
4. Add Decay Time Check to arena_maybe_decay_muzzy()
Modify in src/arena.c:

```c
static void
arena_maybe_decay_muzzy(tsdn_t *tsdn, arena_t *arena,
    bool is_background_thread) {
    // Add early exit if decay is disabled
    if (arena->decay_muzzy.time_ms == -1) {
        return;
    }

    // Existing logic
    if (arena->decay_muzzy.time_ms > 0) {
        arena_decay_to_limit(tsdn, arena, &arena->decay_muzzy,
            &arena->extents_muzzy, is_background_thread, 0,
            arena->decay_muzzy.ceil_npages);
    }
}
```
**Key Changes Explained:**

_Decoupled Decay Logic:_

Muzzy decay now runs every time dirty decay runs
Removed the conditional check that required dirty decay to complete first

_Independent Background Processing:_

Added dedicated muzzy decay path in background threads
Ensures periodic processing even without dirty page pressure

_Explicit Disable Check:_

Added explicit guard for time_ms = -1 (disable)
Makes behavior more predictable

But jemalloc seems to be not maintained anymore? Archived in github.
Maybe @interwq can advise? This also has been asked [here](https://github.com/jemalloc/jemalloc/issues/2800#issuecomment-2722659156) by @orlp .

2) **Keep muzzy_decay_ms disabled, but expose jemalloc_purge()  to polars users**:
```rust

use jemalloc_ctl::{epoch, raw};

fn jemalloc_purge() {
    // Advance epoch to flush stats
    epoch::advance().expect("Failed to advance jemalloc epoch");

    // Purge all arenas
    let purge_result = unsafe {
        raw::write(b"arena.0.decay\0", ())
    };

    // For multi-arena systems:
    if purge_result.is_err() {
        let _ = unsafe { raw::write(b"arenas.all.decay\0", ()) };
    }
}
```

or similar.

So that we could call pl.jemalloc_purge() after heavy memory operations and be fast while having no OOMs and using memory efficiently.

Also maybe we could create some background thread that checks current RSS periodically and calls jemalloc_purge if needed.

3) **Switching to another allocator?**


Overall, the test 

```python
arr = np.random.randn(1000000)
arrp = pl.Series(arr)
%timeit arrp - 1
```

that has lead to such cardinal change in memory management, it simply does not seem reflecting real use cases of Polars to me.
I did not notice, maybe whole benchmakring suites were run somewhere with muzzy_decay_ms enable vs disabled?
If not, I'm not sure there is significant drop in performance that compensates for troubles introduced by disabling muzzy_decay_ms.
